{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight","id":981972,"title":"[2E New Stuff][Help] Blood Sight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-04T22:36:23-07:00","id":981972,"title":"[2E New Stuff][Help] Blood Sight","content":"So, I wrote a thing inspired by some story about a vamp who saw the sunrise. Auspex is cool and all, but I'm a sucker for sweet eyewear and Darth Kreia from Knights of the Old Republic 2, so having blindfolded vampires running around that &quot;See beyond sight&quot; is appealing. Problem is, I'm having some trouble coming up with some specifics. I've got some basic ideas and a short writeup. But I don't have anything substantial.<br /> <br /> \u201cI saw the sun...\u201d<br /> \u201cIt was glorious; beautiful. I hadn\u2019t seen it in decades. It was an accident, of course. I spent the night with my grandson. He was on his deathbed. AIDS left him a shell of his former self. I didn\u2019t trust him to make it to the next night, so I had to...at any rate, by the time I made it back to my Haven, the dawn had started to creep over the horizon, and I looked heavenward at just the right moment. I managed to resist the Beast\u2019s fear, but my eyes burned out of their sockets before I had the chance to retreat to my chambers.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe next evening, my eyes were still gone, and I was hungry. A servant gave their lifeblood to me. But I couldn\u2019t concentrate. I decided not to grow my eyes back. I could, if I wanted to. But I choose not to. It\u2019s a reminder of our weakness, but also our strength. I see so much more without them, and I shall never forget my last sunrise.\u201d<br /> <br /> Blood Sight<br /> This unique form of Cru\u00e1c was developed by a member of the Circle of the Crone whose eyes were burned out by the sun. It doesn\u2019t require its Acolytes to go to such extremes, but since blinding oneself is required in the ritual, the Acolyte gouging her eyes out is a common practice among older practitioners (though spending a Vitae in any other fashion is acceptable). If a queasy Kindred blindfolds herself, then as soon as the blindfold is removed, the effect ends until she casts the spell again. Otherwise, it lasts until the Kindred\u2019s eyes regrow during daysleep.<br /> <br /> The simplest benefit of Bloodsight is that the Acolyte\u2019s Kindred Senses treat her Blood Potency as 2 higher. In addition, the Acolyte gains Unseen Senses (Ephemeral Entities).<br /> <br /> And after that point I don't really know where to go. Sight beyond sight, enhanced other senses. Makes sense for vampires. Just trying to come up with something more interesting. Seeing through Concealment definitely. But maybe this should be some sort of Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:13:04-07:00","id":982008,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, so lets run with this!<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Bloodsight</b><br /> <br /> The Bloodsight has it's origins in an Acolyte who was burnt by sunlight, but the Acolytes know that is in darkness their kind belongs. The act of blinding oneself opens the faithful to truths their eyes deny, human senses keeping the Acolyte from achieving true connection with her true nature. The Beast dwells in a shroud of eternal blackness, and by caging herself within that realm with it, the Acolytes believe they can listen to it unlike any other.<br /> <br /> <b>Emboldening the Hunter (\u2022):</b> Your character has ritually blinded herself in hopes of growing closer to her inner darkness, empowering the Beast. She doubles the base range of all her Kindred Senses (see Vampire the Requiem 2nd Edition, p. 91).<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Will Tell (\u2022\u2022):</b> Your character's Beast isn't just emboldened, but an experienced hunter of men and monsters, fully capable of replacing her lost sight with something more. If tracking by blood your character suffers a \u20132 die penalty to rolls that require vision to act against her prey, and if the vampire tastes her victim's blood she suffers no penalty at all. This does not allow the character to see her target.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>The Beast has learned to see all as prey, a source of nourishment essential to survival, and this mindset has slowly crept into the character's own instincts. Whenever she tastes a Kindred victim's vitae a vampire with this merit must roll Resolve + Composure, minus one die for each point of vitae taken. Failure means she will feed on her prey to the bitter end, should she successfully subdue it.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Union (\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Your character understands her Beast in such a way that it can almost make sense of it, at times. She understands what makes it tick, and in return it has grown overzealous of the vampire. Anytime the character Lashes Out (see Vampire the Requiem 2nd Edition, p. 92) she may add her dots in this merit to the roll.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> A Beast unleashed is a dangerous partner. It knows only the need to feed and protect the vampire, and in any scene the character has Lashed Out all her rolls to resist frency (but not ride it) are penalized by this merit's dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Beckoning Shadows (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>The terrifying truth is that most Kindred believe themselves to be apex predators because they cannot feel their hunters' presence, hiding among them within stolen bodies. A character with this merit was revealed these terrible truths by her Beast, and may sense the Bird of Dis with a Wits + Blood Potency roll, whether the creature is housed inside a body or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":11263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","user":"Gimmisky","date":". 10-05-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:42:27-07:00","id":982120,"title":"","content":"I dislike the picture here. While boosting kindred senses is cool, and then we can have a blind vampire going off from smelling blood and all that is awesome, the idea that he somehow &quot;sees&quot; is a little bit less cool, at least in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:43:46-07:00","id":982121,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11263_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11263\" data-vbnamecard=\"11263\">Gimmisky</a>, that's a nice Merit. I particularly like Beckoning Shadows, even though my knee-jerk reaction was to reject it.<br /> <br /> I also dig Dark Union, though I'm not sure if it belongs in a Merit about enhanced senses. Combined with Atrocious, Cutthroat, or Enticing it could make for a potent Lashing Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:48:25-07:00","id":982123,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar294_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"294\" data-vbnamecard=\"294\">Griautis</a> While I get that the drawback of being &quot;mundanely blind&quot; is potent, I feel like vampires have enough ways to get around it that it's not a huge issue. Plus, I hear everybody's a fan of this Daredevil show, so take some Parkour and Brawl Merits and you can sell it as &quot;Play Vampire Daredevil.&quot; Also, Vampires always have the opportunity to just grow their eyes back. If they decide they don't like the merit anymore, they just get their eyes back and Sanctity of Merits refunds the XP. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:50:48-07:00","id":982204,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1923_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1923\" data-vbnamecard=\"1923\">BigDamnHero</a> The idea behind the merit was that a blind Kindred would hone more than just her senses, but also empower her Beast by relying more on it to survive than ever before. Upon realizing that the whole Bloodsight thing would have become a quasi-religious proceedure in the Circle, and although that remains the name of the merit, it is more than just &quot;enhanced senses&quot; ability. It is a true communion with the Beast in a very intimate sense. I even had the idea of adding as the Drawback of the last level that the Vampire cannot regenerate her eyes anymore. The Beast is too jealous and cannot let her vampire go.<br /> <br /> That being said, it is just an idea! Tinker with it and see what suits your needs! Also phoneposting is terrible. =|","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":11263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","user":"Gimmisky","date":". 10-05-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:19:46-07:00","id":982220,"title":"","content":"Actually they regrow involuntarily during each Daysleep unless the WP is spent to make it permanent. Then there's no going back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:28:54-07:00","id":982225,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the specific wording doesn't say that they <i>can't</i> go back. That being said, perhaps they just let their eyes grow back and regouge them every night. Or use blindfolds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:40:28-07:00","id":982235,"title":"","content":"Or maybe their ritual messes up with that system in some way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:40:46-07:00","id":982236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982120#post982120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike the picture here. While boosting kindred senses is cool, and then we can have a blind vampire going off from smelling blood and all that is awesome, the idea that he somehow &quot;sees&quot; is a little bit less cool, at least in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, allowing the vampire to see while does seem less awesome and cool than the simple increases to Kindred Senses.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight#post981972\">The simplest benefit of Bloodsight is that the Acolyte\u2019s Kindred Senses treat her Blood Potency as 2 higher. In addition, the Acolyte gains Unseen Senses (Ephemeral Entities).</a><br /> <br /> Also for some reason this seems more a Thesban Miracle than Cruac Ritual. The Cuac only requires spilled blood and ritual, Thesban requires sacrifice, in this case the user's eyes, and Will. This story seems to indicate the latter, and fits themes of humanity, shame, guilt, and acceptance of hardship/lowly-station which run much deeper in the Lance and seems antithetical to the Crone.<br /> <br /> I'd work it as a Condition, which is Resolved by regrowing the eyes, not a Merit. I think having a 'Condition' instead of 'Merit', keeps the dark connotation of suffering for power, and also since it can be removed simply by regrowing the eyes it is temporary/persistent as a Condition and shouldn't be used as a place to Store XP via the sanctity of merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-05-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:55:28-07:00","id":982244,"title":"","content":"I guess it could be a Miracle instead. I like it working as a Condition, too. And like Gimmisky said, maybe it's a special Condition that keeps the eyes from regrowing &quot;naturally&quot;, but doesn't stop them from coming back after the Condition is resolved.<br /> <br /> So, I know that I only talked about enhancing their Kindred Senses and giving them Unseen Senses, but I wanted to give them something else on top of that. Something more mystical but that didn't edge in on Auspex's territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:21:02-07:00","id":982302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982244#post982244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I know that I only talked about enhancing their Kindred Senses and giving them Unseen Senses, but I wanted to give them something else on top of that. Something more mystical but that didn't edge in on Auspex's territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>What power level of the associated Discipline are we talking about, 3, 4 or 5?<br /> <br /> The &quot;Ephemeral Beings&quot; Unseen Sense is already pretty amazing if interpreted as any Ephemeral Being, which is a very broad category of threats including Angels, Ghosts,Spirits, Strix, some Abyssal Intrusions, Arcanum Summoning Beings, and whatever weird other categories/one-offs the storyteller dreams up, in their plethora of Manifestations. If I was going to add anything it'd be the ability to also have Unseen Sense: Portal/Gates to <i>Other </i>Realms.<br /> <br /> Auspex doesn't even touch that stuff, so overlap .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-05-2016, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:52:23-07:00","id":982324,"title":"","content":"If done as a merit line... I would likely follow a similar path as mystery cult initiation. <br /> <br /> Set a Prerequisite.<br /> Burn/pluck out eyes. Do not heal the wound level.<br /> If it is healed, a ritual must be preformed to restore the use of the merit (narrative ritual)<br /> <br /> Then just give a similar benefit value per dot as mystery cult. <br /> <br /> I like the Gimmisky took. Though the 4th dot I probably would have made the 5th dot. And 4th dot would probably give something similar to the unseen sense merit. Or even medium. <br /> <br /> The 3rd rank has me slightly concerned.. could be stacked with Kerebos merit for some serious munchkin powah<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:59:26-07:00","id":982329,"title":"","content":"I think this is focused too much on the &quot;volunteerly pluck out your eyes.&quot;. I think it works better if it simply has a prerequisite &quot;Blind&quot;. How that came to be is another matter and left up to the story - it has probably been developed by a Blind Lancea Priest, but that doesn't stop others from blinding themselves purposely to get this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:15:45-07:00","id":982387,"title":"","content":"Udjat is an Auspex 2 devotion... (Khaibit Bloodline Gift, but others can learn it) and lets you see while blinded... and allows for seeing ephemeral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:20:31-07:00","id":982504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982387#post982387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Udjat is an Auspex 2 devotion... (Khaibit Bloodline Gift, but others can learn it) and lets you see while blinded... and allows for seeing ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can people learn a Bloodline's Devotions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T01:06:10-07:00","id":982591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982504#post982504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Can people learn a Bloodline's Devotions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. The devotions like obtenebration are exclusive to the bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T02:38:38-07:00","id":982608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982591#post982591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No. The devotions like obtenebration are exclusive to the bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they aren't. Bloodlines get the foundation power for free (Udjat for Khaibit) everyone else not in the bloodline has to meet the pre requisites and pay for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T03:24:00-07:00","id":982626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982608#post982608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they aren't. Bloodlines get the foundation power for free (Udjat for Khaibit) everyone else not in the bloodline has to meet the pre requisites and pay for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 98 of the 2e core. bloodlines possess &quot;unique Disciplines, exclusive Devotions or strange sorceries.&quot; as well it later says &quot;nobody outside the bloodline can learn their gift, even through diablerie.&quot; That makes it pretty clear to me that all forms of bloodline gifts are meant to be unique to members of the bloodline and unable to be learned by those not in the bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T04:46:25-07:00","id":982640,"title":"","content":"Yep also on page 84, the wrap over text from 83 about learning disciplines. Last sentence. <br /> <br /> Kindred may not learn the signature disciplines of bloodlines even through diablerie. <br /> <br /> Probably really meant it if they wrote it twice in 1 book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:08:51-07:00","id":982649,"title":"","content":"1) Obtenebration is no longer a discipline. Its a series of devotions. Different rules apply. There has never been a rule that says bloodline merits, rituals, or devotions are off limits, even in 1e. Furthermore, <i>this is a crown. A completely new type of mechanic that is not in the core book. Things are clearly different.</i><br /> <br /> 2) We've had David Hill, the man who wrote up the new Khaibit as well as a major Vampire writer<i>, </i>say that non-Khaibit can buy the Obtenebration disciplines. Death of the author and all, though, so its not like there's police to force you to do anything. But it does lend some weight.<br /> <br /> 3) Even if you want to forbid the devotions... If you're making a custom power anyways, what difference does it make if you have to make a devotion that's slightly tweaked than a narrowly used ritual? Why reinvent the wheel when the solution is right there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-06-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:58:36-07:00","id":982722,"title":"","content":"I'd go with you can learn bloodline devotions but some would be very well guarded and the members of the bloodline would not like seeing ''strangers'' using those devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:29:55-07:00","id":982738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982649#post982649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Obtenebration is no longer a discipline. Its a series of devotions. Different rules apply. There has never been a rule that says bloodline merits, rituals, or devotions are off limits, even in 1e. Furthermore, <i>this is a crown. A completely new type of mechanic that is not in the core book. Things are clearly different.</i><br /> <br /> 2) We've had David Hill, the man who wrote up the new Khaibit as well as a major Vampire writer<i>, </i>say that non-Khaibit can buy the Obtenebration disciplines. Death of the author and all, though, so its not like there's police to force you to do anything. But it does lend some weight.<br /> <br /> 3) Even if you want to forbid the devotions... If you're making a custom power anyways, what difference does it make if you have to make a devotion that's slightly tweaked than a narrowly used ritual? Why reinvent the wheel when the solution is right there?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yeah but in 1e they specifically created disciplines. With the few bloodlines they have created it appears they are going away from that. I like it so far, but you would really allow anybody to pick up the heads of Kerebos merit without being a Kerebos?<br /> <br /> 2. Dunno about that. I would have to disagree with him unless I was going to simply remove bloodlines all together and just say, there's lots of weird shit out there. <br /> <br /> 3. True. And it's ok to say no sometimes. I don't like to belittle 1 players work and accepting the baggage of a bloodline just to have another pc or npc for that matter get it at no real cost. That is why bloodline banes are advised to be much more harsh in 2e. <br /> <br /> OP play it as you want. My advice is treat bloodline perks as sacred. And make the penalty harsh. Makes players really have to want something and commit to it. Makes it really part of their character and not just some new flashy power they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:15:30-07:00","id":982771,"title":"","content":"EDIT - just a fact check.<br /> <br /> There were a number of bloodlines that had only a fourth, core book discipline and a handful of devotions. <u><i>Most</i></u> had a fourth bloodline disicipline, but that is not universally true. For example, there's the Nelapsi off the top of my head. Got Nightmare as a fourth discipline, and could create three devotions. Theoretically, anyone could learn them, but it necessitated finding a teacher, which could prove difficult.<br /> <br /> As for the number of releases? It means nothing; there are countless reasons why they could have stopped publishing bloodlines on the blog. Maybe saving for the books. We don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-06-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:29:42-07:00","id":982774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/981972-2e-new-stuff-help-blood-sight?p=982771#post982771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT - just a fact check.<br /> <br /> There were a number of bloodlines that had only a fourth, core book discipline and a handful of devotions. <u><i>Most</i></u> had a fourth bloodline disicipline, but that is not universally true. For example, there's the Nelapsi off the top of my head. Got Nightmare as a fourth discipline, and could create three devotions. Theoretically, anyone could learn them, but it necessitated finding a teacher, which could prove difficult.<br /> <br /> As for the number of releases? It means nothing; there are countless reasons why they could have stopped publishing bloodlines on the blog. Maybe saving for the books. We don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can hope <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> New bloodline book plz lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}